<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Llibre dels fets</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">13th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Book of Deeds</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Llibre dels fets ('Book of Deeds') is the chronicle of the reign of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-i-of-aragon">James I of Aragon</a>, the Conqueror, dictated in Catalan by the king himself. Recounting his conquests of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mallorca">Majorca</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valencia">Valencia</a> in the first person, it is the first of the four great Catalan chronicles and one of the earliest autobiographies by a medieval Christian king.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/llibre-dels-fets.jpg" alt="Llibre dels fets" width="320" height="484" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Celestí des Torrents · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Llibre-dels-Feyts-XXVIIr.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
